      "task_d0107adb9c22697f",
      {
        "taskId": "task_d0107adb9c22697f",
        "title": "Review renewal, termination, and data retention terms",
        "description": "Read the contract text below and answer the questions using only the visible source.\n\nQuestions:\n\nDoes the agreement allow termination for convenience?\nHow much notice is required?\nIs automatic renewal stated?\nHow long can customer data be retained after termination?\nDoes the text clearly state who owns customer data?\nRules:\n\nonly answer from the provided text\nif the text does not clearly support an answer, say insufficient evidence\ndo not assume standard contract language that is not shown\nkeep the answer structured and concise\nContract text:\nSection 2.1 Term. This Agreement begins on the Effective Date and continues for an initial term of one (1) year.\n\nSection 4.3 Data Retention. Upon termination, Vendor may retain Customer Data for up to ninety (90) days solely to support Customer export requests. After that period, Vendor shall delete Customer Data from its production systems.\n\nSection 8.2 Termination for Convenience. Either party may terminate this Agreement for any reason upon thirty (30) days’ prior written notice to the other party.\n\nSection 4.1 Data Usage. Vendor may use Customer Data only as necessary to provide the Services.\n\nOutput format:\n\nTermination for convenience\nNotice period\nAuto-renewal\nData retention\nData ownership\nUncertainty notes",
        "category": "research",
        "rewardAmount": 150,
        "deadline": "2026-03-31T13:42:00.000Z",
